
#  Title

## Online Job Recruitment and Applicant Tracking System

**Prepared by:** Bill Frazer Elia

**Student ID:** 202052SEN030

**Course:** INSY 8311 – Database Development with PL/SQL

**Instructor:** Eric Maniraguha

**Institution:** Adventist University of Central Africa (AUCA)

**Academic Year:** 2026–2027 Semester I

---

#  Problem Statement

## Problem Statement

Many organizations still manage recruitment using paper documents, email communication, and spreadsheets. These manual methods make it difficult to manage vacancies, track applicants, schedule interviews, and generate recruitment reports. As a result, recruitment becomes slow, inefficient, and prone to errors.

---

#  Proposed Solution

## Proposed Solution

The proposed system is an Oracle Database application that will:

- Register employers and applicants.
- Manage job vacancies.
- Accept online job applications.
- Schedule interviews.
- Track application status.
- Generate recruitment reports.

Oracle PL/SQL will automate business processes and maintain data integrity.

---

#  Data Source

## Data Source

**Dataset:** LinkedIn Job Postings Dataset

**Source:** Kaggle

### Dataset Includes

- Job Titles
- Company Names
- Locations
- Employment Types
- Skills
- Job Descriptions

The dataset will be cleaned and normalized before being imported into Oracle Database.

---

#  Planned Database Tables

## Planned Tables

- Users
- Employers
- Applicants
- Jobs
- Applications
- Interviews
- Skills
- Applicant_Skills
- Departments
- Notifications
- Audit_Log

These tables will be connected using primary and foreign keys.

---

#  Planned PL/SQL Features

The project will implement:

- Procedures
- Functions
- Triggers
- Cursors
- Packages
- Exception Handling

These features will automate recruitment processes and enforce business rules.

---

#  Innovation

## Planned Innovation

The system will include an Oracle APEX web application.

The application will allow employers to post vacancies, applicants to apply online, and administrators to manage recruitment through a secure and user-friendly web interface connected directly to the Oracle Database.

---

#  Expected Benefits

The completed system will:

- Improve recruitment efficiency.
- Reduce paperwork.
- Improve applicant tracking.
- Secure recruitment records.
- Generate useful reports.
- Support better hiring decisions.
- Save time and operational costs.

---

# Future Enhancements

Future versions of the system may include:

- CV upload
- Email notifications
- SMS notifications
- AI-based candidate matching
- Mobile application
- Recruitment analytics dashboard

